                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e2fc942a-a32d-3407-9a3f-149ba7ef3107",
                        "entry_id": "30a2bec8-e831-3ef7-8878-33ef717992cb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The quality of being sweet or pleasing to the mind; agreeableness; pleasantness"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "86fc95e0-398c-4e45-820d-cbcc0a790c90",
                                "sense_id": "e2fc942a-a32d-3407-9a3f-149ba7ef3107",
                                "text": "suavity of manners"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f69cb660-784f-4d4f-a7a5-dc0f9f188335",
                                "sense_id": "e2fc942a-a32d-3407-9a3f-149ba7ef3107",
                                "text": "suavity of language, conversation, or address"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "76aee77a-e88c-4d67-948b-a71673562b81",
                                "sense_id": "e2fc942a-a32d-3407-9a3f-149ba7ef3107",
                                "text": "[N]othing, not even the crude curves of the railway, can utterly deform the suavity of contour of one bay after another along the whole reach of the Riviera."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "49ea9f58-f118-467e-8dfc-488452cf137e",
                                "sense_id": "e2fc942a-a32d-3407-9a3f-149ba7ef3107",
                                "text": "[T]he brothers’ gowns and broad straw hats were hanging up, each with his religious name upon a board,—names full of legendary suavity and interest, such as Basil, Hilarion, Raphael, or Pacifique; […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b69280d5-d0cd-3616-84f2-8627cb65e9a5",
                        "entry_id": "30a2bec8-e831-3ef7-8878-33ef717992cb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The quality of being suave."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0c2d0d37-e281-4e40-ad93-11e4812a8918",
                                "sense_id": "b69280d5-d0cd-3616-84f2-8627cb65e9a5",
                                "text": "Macavity, Macavity, there’s no one like Macavity,\nThere never was a Cat of such deceitfulness and suavity."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1e369463-5227-3852-8537-5078df03847b",
                        "entry_id": "30a2bec8-e831-3ef7-8878-33ef717992cb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Sweetness or agreeableness to the senses, especially of taste and odour."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "obsolete",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9da4072b-1425-478e-a085-6f2b4e6c6aa2",
                                "sense_id": "1e369463-5227-3852-8537-5078df03847b",
                                "text": "Whan this ſayd monument diſcouered was / Suche a ſuauite and fragrant odoure / Aſcended from the corps by ſingular grace / Paſſyng all worldly ſwetnes and ſauour / That all there present that day and hour / Suppoſed they had ben / in the felicite / Of erthely paradiſe / without ambiguite."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "31f715da-d2a0-4375-b97c-5ffc0df80cc2",
                        "source_entry_id": "30a2bec8-e831-3ef7-8878-33ef717992cb",
                        "source_sense_description": "the quality of being sweet or pleasing to the mind",
                        "target_lang_word": "hoflijkheid",
                        "target_lang_code": "nl",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "70439ead-0b80-488e-b050-cec42d06bb4c",
                        "source_entry_id": "30a2bec8-e831-3ef7-8878-33ef717992cb",
                        "source_sense_description": "the quality of being sweet or pleasing to the mind",
                        "target_lang_word": "courtoisie",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "courtoisie",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "33247251-4971-3d5d-8f27-2fb64a78a66d",
                                        "entry_id": "cba9333b-6577-3468-951b-abb107b8dafa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Manière de parler et d’agir de celui qui est courtois."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "84df0e71-f067-4100-8574-4d9d3a2c61df",
                                                "sense_id": "33247251-4971-3d5d-8f27-2fb64a78a66d",
                                                "text": "Pour ma première au bordel, c’est la patronne qui se chargea de mon accueil. Après les courtoisies d’usage, elle me fit prendre place dans un des fauteuils confortables du salon, avant de m’inviter à avaler une rasade d’absinthe : pour te décontracter !, lança-t-elle."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd8eebcf-00fa-4f80-8c0e-91c8dfdf9808",
                                                "sense_id": "33247251-4971-3d5d-8f27-2fb64a78a66d",
                                                "text": "La langue de la courtoisie, reprit Rowena, quand on l’emploie pour cacher la grossièreté des actions, ressemble à la ceinture d’un chevalier qui ceint la taille d’un vil manant."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "17dd9262-36fe-493d-99a0-b1e71837dccf",
                                                "sense_id": "33247251-4971-3d5d-8f27-2fb64a78a66d",
                                                "text": "Le ton, les modes, les façons de Paris y dominent ; et de l’ancienne vie flamande, les Douaisiens n’auront plus bientôt que la cordialité des soins hospitaliers, la courtoisie espagnole, la richesse et la propreté de la Hollande."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f9f9a016-9118-45aa-acb3-0308d00df53a",
                                                "sense_id": "33247251-4971-3d5d-8f27-2fb64a78a66d",
                                                "text": "Silence, voyons, dit le maire. Chacun doit écouter avec courtoisie l’adversaire, même s’il est de mauvaise foi, même s’il manque de civilité ! Exprimons-nous poliment. Rétorquons de même, sans nous départir de sang-froid."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "614dd60c-de78-4a6d-a80a-dedca0862e93",
                                                "sense_id": "33247251-4971-3d5d-8f27-2fb64a78a66d",
                                                "text": "Il souriait même en dormant, dans la nuit la plus noire, par courtoisie envers la lumière, et envers son contraire."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
